how to use/ translation to JS

Core rules

1. Indentation defines blocks (no `{ }` in source)
2. Newlines end statements
3. Strings use "double quotes".
4. Time is in seconds (`wait 1`, `loop 2`) → emitted JS uses milliseconds
5. Program starts with app Name
6. On load, the engine creates the app and auto-calls `"run", "start", or init if present.
7. print -> browser/Node Console (`console.log`)
8. put … in "id" changes text on the page (element `id`).
9. let`is for movement (`let "hero" forward`), NOT normal variables as 
